struct Point {
    int x;
    int y;
}

//KNOWN BUG (Phase 4 gap, surfaced 2026-08-08 P3 audit):
//AllocArrayOnHeap initializes struct-array elements to 0 (null heap
//idx) instead of materializing a fresh Point on the heap for each
//element. So `arr[0].x = 1` evaluates arr[0] -> 0, then StoreField
//with heapIdx=0 fails the bounds check at VmExecutor.cpp:659.
//
//Test currently "passes" because the runtime throw exits with code 1,
//which coincidentally matches the manifest's expected exit. The
//semantic intent is `return arr[1].x` = 3.
//
//Fix requires design decision: eager materialization at alloc_array
//(walk elements, AllocStructOnHeap for each) vs. lazy at first access
//(load_element detects struct-element-kind and allocates on demand).
//GC interaction must be considered either way.
//
//Tracked in memory: nlang-array-of-struct-bug.md.
int main() {
    Point[] arr = new Point[2];
    arr[0].x = 1;
    arr[0].y = 2;
    arr[1].x = 3;
    arr[1].y = 4;
    return arr[1].x;
}

